# BoronDNS Debian package

The package installs the static MUSL BoronDNS and BoronGun executables, creates
the `borondns` service account, and enables `borondns.service`. The service has
`ConditionPathExists=/etc/borondns-secondary/config.toml`, so a new installation
remains inactive until an operator installs a valid configuration.

Start the service after configuring it:

```sh
sudo install -m 0640 -o root -g borondns config.toml \
  /etc/borondns-secondary/config.toml
sudo systemctl start borondns
```

Package removal and purge preserve `/var/lib/borondns`, including zone cache
data. Remove that directory explicitly only when its operational data is no
longer required.

The archive installer and this package use different executable locations.
Remove or migrate an archive install, including its locally managed
`/etc/systemd/system/borondns.service`, before installing this package.

## Building a package

`scripts/package-deb.sh` takes the upstream version from
`workspace.package.version` in `Cargo.toml`. A release tag must be `v` followed
by that version. GitHub tag refs, an explicit `BORONDNS_RELEASE_TAG`, and local
release tags at HEAD are checked when available. For a source archive without
Git metadata, pass `BORONDNS_RELEASE_TAG=vX.Y.Z` to check the intended tag.

`BORONDNS_DEB_VERSION`, if set, must match Cargo; it cannot rename a release.
Use `BORONDNS_DEB_REVISION` for packaging-only revisions. Both input executables
must run on the build host and report the same upstream version with `--version`.
The lifecycle test derives its package filenames and stub versions from the
same source, and checks the installed package version after install and upgrade.
